  "limitations": [
    "The prior Foundation-Sequence-Lifetime-Runner.exe rejected the same published candidate with exit 1 and phase=envelope. It was not expected to pass the new runtime selection.",
    "The host envelope authenticates minor 39 through the complete verifier before candidate parsing. Request major 1 and existing portable/capability-free/scanner limits remain required. The separate browser envelope is unchanged.",
    "The invalid variants cover unknown version/opcode, zero/unknown projection, wrong owner/view type, borrowed-parameter read, ownership-taking use, and truncation. This is not exhaustive malformed-module qualification.",
    "Both native packages use one Windows-built runner WVB. No independent Linux compiler reconstruction or fresh compilation of the pinned candidate source was performed.",
    "Sequence regressions use WVB 1.28 and do not establish arbitrary borrowed Sequence/Vector/callable payload execution. Remaining payload integration and a maintained real consumer are still required.",
    "The automatic plan proposed three broad owners with 2130 expected seconds. Focused current-runner construction and execution were selected; unchanged verifier component results were retained. Broad front-door, callable, bootstrap, WebAssembly, OS, installed-tool, and complete qualification suites were not run.",
    "No complete Option/Result, exclusive-borrow, take, mapping, installed-tool promotion, or compiler/library goal completion is claimed.",
    "The full existing owner now invokes these ten runtime cases after constructing its runner; its registered total rises from 539 to 549. The complete 549-case owner was not run in this checkpoint. Focused runtime execution was repeated after this orchestration edit, reusing unchanged runner packages."
